  <p>Every bird in this table is captive-bred in the USA with full documentation. <a href="https://www.cites.org/eng/app/appendices.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The CITES appendices</a> have carried African Greys on Appendix I since the CoP17 uplisting took effect in January 2017, which is the strictest tier the convention has, and it is why paperwork matters more in this species than in almost anything else you could put in an aviary. <a href="/congo-african-grey-for-sale/">Our Congo African Grey listings</a> carry the same documentation on the single birds.</p>

