             per page; remaining productive years stays a card element, not a second module. -->
        <section id="checklist">
          <h2 class="cag-h2">Which Six Questions Separate a Proven Pair From a Claimed One?</h2>
          <p class="lead">Every question below can be answered by any honest seller in about a minute, and none of them requires trusting us. Run the list against our three pairs, then run it against the next listing you open. The point is not that we score well; it is that most listings cannot answer question one.</p>

          <h3 class="cag-h3">Six Questions to Ask Before You Pay</h3>
          <p>Tick each one you can get a straight answer to. The tally underneath tells you what you are actually looking at, and nothing you enter leaves your browser.</p>

          <div class="chk">
            <p class="chk-k">Is This Pair Actually Proven?</p>
            <p class="chk-sub">Six questions · tick the ones the seller can answer</p>
            <ul class="chk-list">
              <li><label><input type="checkbox" data-chk><span>Has this pair hatched a fertile clutch, and when?</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox" data-chk><span>How old is each bird?</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox" data-chk><span>Are both birds closed-banded, and what are the band numbers?</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox" data-chk><span>Can you see the clutch record before you pay?</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox" data-chk><span>Is the pair sold together, and never split?</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox" data-chk><span>Will the seller say what happens if the pair stops producing after the move?</span></label></li>
            </ul>
            <div class="chk-out" id="chkOut" role="status" aria-live="polite">
              <p class="chk-score" id="chkScore">0 of 6 answered</p>
              <p class="chk-verdict" id="chkVerdict">Tick a question once you have a straight answer to it.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h4 class="cag-h4">What a Straight Answer Looks Like</h4>
          <p>A straight answer carries a date, a number, or a plain no. "Yes, proven" is not an answer to question one; "she hatched three in the spring of last year and two the spring before, and I will send you the dates" is. When a seller answers question six with silence, that silence is the answer, and it is worth more than anything in the listing photos.</p>
          <p>We answer all six on this page, in public, before anyone asks. Talker and Jane have four hatched clutches with dates, Mari and Lake two, Sally and Odin one. Both birds in each pair wear closed bands we can read out over the phone. No pair here is ever split. And on question six, our answer is the one nobody likes giving: we do not promise a clutch, because no honest breeder can — what we promise is the method we use to move a pair and the fact that we will stay on the phone with you while it settles.</p>

          <p class="ctaline"><a href="#reserve" class="btn-clay">Ask for the clutch record</a></p>
        </section>

